          "collection_date": "2020",
          "description": {
            "comment": "Genome assembly Wolbachia endosymbiont of Phyllotreta cruciferae. HiFiasm used to assemble HiFi reads and haplotigs purged. Manual curation and Hi-C to bring to chromosome level. HiFiasm does produce complete chromosome haplotigs for many of the chromosomes for this species, as it's a small genome. Suggest future update to would be to rerun haplotig assembly software like hifiasm or others and reannotate haplotype version. Single primary sequence assembly, not haplotype assembled. Single individual, unknown sex used for HiFi PacBio and Hi-C Illumina reads. Mixed sample with Phyllotreta striolata but one individual taken that is correct species. Taken from Canada in September 2020.",
